The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
timeout = nf_flowtable_time_stamp + flow_offload_get_timeout(flow);
if (READ_ONCE(flow->timeout) != timeout)
```
Reason:
The code checks if the current timeout has changed and attempts to offload the flow without any delay or limit on the retry attempts. This results in continuous retries as quickly as possible after a failure, leading to excessive system load.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (timeout - READ_ONCE(flow->timeout) > HZ)
    WRITE_ONCE(flow->timeout, timeout);
else
    return;
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a condition that limits the flow timeout update and hardware offload retry to once per second (defined by `HZ`). This prevents excessive retries by ensuring that the flow can only be retried if the timeout has exceeded one second since the last attempt, thereby reducing system load.

